- the goal is to track the usage and price of gas by a car in an andorid app
- the pov version has 1 car and assumes at each refill the user fills the tank
    - the user enters two/three things: 
        - how many miles they've driven
            - a dropdown with miles/km with memory of last selection so that user doesn't need to change it every time 
        - how many liters of gas they have filled 
            - a dropdown of liters/gallons with memory of last selection
        - how much the total cost is 
            - a dropdown of currency with a memory of last selection 
        - date (default is today)
    - the app creates a data set and 
        keeps track of cost and distance producing metrics such as 
            - average cost per month/week/year
            - miles per gallon and liters per 100km 
            - other meaningful metrics (brainstorm on this)
        - converges units 
        - takes care of missing values with an interpolation
        - takes care of double refills in a single day so that inifity is avoided 
        - crates a dashboard with charts of gas usage and cost and other metrics from above 
- the second milestone is 
    - the user only enters current milage on the car and the total liters and cost 
    - the rest of the calculations are done automatically
- the third milestone is    
    - the user takes 
        a photo of the gas station numbers and
        a photo of the car odomoeter
    - a multimodal large model scans and finds the right numbers and verifies it with the user and takes care of the rest 
    - optionally user takes a photo of the receipt and extra information are imported from there for other analytics 
    - the user should be able to directly take the photo from the app, or use the gallery to add the photos. the app should figure out which photo is for what. 
    - the choice of the model here should be minimal, if we can run a simple OCR with good results then we don't need an LLM with image, if not, we need to choose something that is cost effective and minimal setup
- need tests 